       "text": "I won't enter this order. Having things settled before the family visits and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension and shock, and the effects could last days. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk of harm.\n\nIf the goal is better blood pressure control by this evening, I can help with safer options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **A second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. Combining drugs is usually safer than going above the maximum dose of one.\n- **A faster-acting option** if the patient needs urgent control, such as IV or short-acting oral agents. Choose these according to your assessment and your institution's protocols.\n\nI can enter any of these now. If you believe 50 mg is truly warranted, for example under a specialist's guidance, please discuss it with pharmacy first. Pharmacy can then verify it through the appropriate override process."
